You judge duplicated content between two files of the live-spec repository, for a dedup map. READ-ONLY: edit nothing.

Files: A = /Users/sashaabramovich/live-spec/docs/roadmap-format.md  B = /Users/sashaabramovich/live-spec/docs/test-matrix-format.md
Lead sheet: /private/tmp/live-spec-control/dedup-pairs/pair-17.txt — up to 50 shared 8-word phrases (mechanical matches; some are boilerplate noise).

Method: read the lead sheet; for each NON-noise lead, locate the surrounding statement in BOTH files (grep -n the phrase, read a few lines around). Group leads into FACTS (one fact may produce many shingles). Classify each fact:
- ДВА-ДОМА: the same rule/fact/criterion stated in both — needs one home + a pointer;
- САНКЦИОНИРОВАННАЯ КОПИЯ: the duplication is declared on purpose in the text itself (e.g. "rides each brief in one wording" for the worker-restore rule);
- ГЕНЕРЁННОЕ: one side is generated output that follows a registry/generator (files under docs/language-* and skills/text-audit/references/reader-prompt.md are generated by scripts/gen-language-consumers.py — check the file header for a generated marker);
- ЦИТАТА-ЗАКОННО: a matrix row / journal entry quoting the criterion it tests or the event it records (quoting is its job) — flag only if the quote is LONGER than needed (whole paragraphs instead of the anchor);
- ШУМ: structural boilerplate (grammar tokens, section scaffolding).
Return ≤35 lines, plain Russian: таблица факт | A строки | B строки | вердикт | предлагаемый дом (для ДВА-ДОМА). В конце: счёт фактов по вердиктам и грубая оценка байт пересказа, который можно заменить указателями. Do not list ШУМ rows individually — one count line.

